      "sourceTextSha256": "8c4ffcd636cfe4c6a7abe3a07a641eee6a8bed12031db63f9f0ca5e17772b2d2",
      "text": "Day 10 · After breakfast, a tour of the White City, a fine example of colonial architecture. Founded by the Spaniards in the 16th century in a fertile valley at more than 2,300 m, surrounded by the Misti, Chachani and Pichu Pichu volcanoes, Arequipa takes its nickname from the white volcanic stone of its buildings, and its historic centre has been a UNESCO World Heritage Site since 2000. Visit the main square, the Yanahuara viewpoint and the Santa Catalina Monastery, founded in the late 16th century, a city within the city of some 20,000 square metres, with a church, galleries, gardens and a gallery of religious art. Transfer to the airport and flight to Lima; transfer to the hotel.",
